  "narrative": "The open ear shows the characteristic ear-canal resonance of roughly +14 dB near 2 kHz relative to 1 kHz. Occluding the ear with a tightly sealed earmold strongly attenuates external sound below 2 kHz (negative REOIG), whereas open and tulip domes provide almost no attenuation. REOIG therefore quantifies coupling tightness and is the acoustic quantity most directly related to the probe-tube presence effect.",
